< https://github.com/tacplus-dev/looper/issues/73#issuecomment-6994085976 https://github.com/tacplus-dev/looper/issues/73
I haven't changed any code. Step 3 (retiring looper-docker and the broker) needs a decision from you first, so I commented on the issue, added `needs-decision`, and stopped as rule 1 asks.

tacplus#340 is closed and tacplus now pins its build image. But the issue's condition that every repository is pinned, and its test, are not met yet:

- **Three repositories have no pin.** `onscreen`, `chaos` and `people` contain only planning files and have approved issues waiting. Once the broker and the unpinned path are gone, their reports would have no `docker` and no `--build`, and their manager could not run any gates. Their first issues could not be verified or landed. `roadmap` has no pin either, but it is docs only and needs nothing.
- **SeaBeam's GitLab instance (currently parked)** would lose its only way to run gates, because build jobs only work for repositories on GitHub.
- **The rootless image-build test can't pass yet.** The pinned build image (2.6.13) has no BuildKit, and tacplus#315 is still open, waiting on tacplus#829 and #830. Until then, a release's image is still built with `docker buildx` on the VM runners.

What I recommended in the comment:
1. The hub adds a `build.lock` to `onscreen`, `chaos` and `people`, and every new repository gets one when it is created.
2. After the retirement, work in an unpinned repository fails at once with "pin it first" rather than falling back to the old path.
3. SeaBeam stays parked, with a PROPOSALS.md entry saying it needs its own way to run build jobs on GitLab first.
4. The removal lands once the three pins are in. The image-build test becomes its own follow-up, blocked by tacplus#315.

The next run does the removal once a member agrees to or changes this and confirms the pins: https://github.com/tacplus-dev/looper/issues/73#issuecomment-6994085976
